# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private workspace
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Design docs, pitches, and decisions live outside the public repo.
.doc/
doc/

# AI assistant workspace (kept local, never pushed)
# `.claude/*` and not `.claude/`: git does not descend into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so
# a negation below a `.claude/` rule can never match. Each level is re-included, then
# re-excluded, so the allowlist at the bottom is reachable.
.claude/*
CLAUDE.md
# Exception: bench/global/docker/**/CLAUDE.md are baked into docker images
# at build time, not the user's local AI context.
!bench/global/docker/**/CLAUDE.md
# Exception: improvement-loop/CLAUDE.md is the bench loop's own rule-book, read by
# the headless phase agents the driver spawns. Same reason the four bench agents are
# tracked: it is load-bearing instructions, not one person's local AI context. The
# ROOT CLAUDE.md stays private - that one is the local context.
!improvement-loop/CLAUDE.md

# ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist: the four bench agents the loop actually spawns are
# tracked, every other agent stays local. These carry load-bearing rubrics - the
# six-branch diagnosis taxonomy, the five definition-of-done checks, the struggle
# read's contract - so a rubric the bench stands on cannot live one `rm` from gone.
# Add a name here only when the driver spawns it; personal review agents do not
# belong in the public repo.
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/bench-evaluator.md
!.claude/agents/bench-struggle-read.md
!.claude/agents/bench-win-confirm.md
!.claude/agents/chore.md

.claude.json
.mcp.json
.opencode/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.cursorignore
.opencode/
opencode.json
.codex/
.aider*
.continue/
.windsurf/
AGENTS.md

